---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Breadcrumbs from "../../components/Breadcrumbs.astro";
import Byline from "../../components/Byline.astro";
import LegalNote from "../../components/LegalNote.astro";
import ThreeNumbersTable from "../../components/ThreeNumbersTable.astro";
import { FEATURED } from "../../lib/briefs";
import { LINKS, CANON_PATHS, linkClass, ext } from "../../lib/links";
import { newsArticleNode } from "../../lib/schema";
import { withBase } from "../../lib/base";

const crumbs = [
  { name: "Home", path: "/" },
  { name: "The Brief", path: "/brief" },
  { name: FEATURED.title, path: FEATURED.path },
];

const pageUrl = "https://fflintel.com/brief/three-numbers";
---

<BaseLayout
  title={`${FEATURED.title} | FFL Intel`}
  description={FEATURED.dek}
  path={FEATURED.path}
  ogImagePath={CANON_PATHS.desk}
  breadcrumbs={crumbs}
  extraJsonLd={[
    newsArticleNode({
      url: pageUrl,
      headline: FEATURED.title,
      description: FEATURED.dek,
      datePublished: FEATURED.date,
      dateModified: FEATURED.date,
      image: `https://fflintel.com/${CANON_PATHS.desk}`,
    }),
  ]}
>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-12 sm:py-14">
    <Breadcrumbs items={crumbs} />
    <p
      class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-sky-400 mb-3"
    >
      {FEATURED.kicker}
    </p>
    <h1
      class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white sm:text-4xl text-balance mb-4"
    >
      {FEATURED.title}
    </h1>
    <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-zinc-300 mb-6">{FEATURED.dek}</p>
    <Byline dateLabel={FEATURED.dateLabel} read={FEATURED.read} />

    <figure class="mt-8 overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-zinc-800">
      <img
        src={withBase(CANON_PATHS.desk)}
        alt={FEATURED.imageAlt}
        width="1280"
        height="720"
        class="w-full"
      />
      <figcaption class="px-4 py-2 text-[11px] text-zinc-500">
        Betsy — the desk.
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        In April, Outdoor Wire put Gearfire’s March print on the wire:
        same-store new firearm units down 11.9 percent from a year earlier,
        down 8.2 percent on the year. I keep that number on a scrap of paper
        because it is a real register series, and because half the people who
        forwarded it treated it like the whole market had spoken.
      </p>
      <p>
        It had not. A same-store panel tells you what rang at a set of stores
        that were open last year and still open this year. That is a better
        sales story than a raw NICS dump. It is still last month. It is still
        only what sold.
      </p>
      <blockquote
        class="border-l-2 border-sky-500/60 pl-4 text-zinc-100 italic"
      >
        A closed period is an after-action report. The scout is the ask — the
        caliber someone typed when the case was empty.
      </blockquote>
      <p>
        I run a small desk, not a second Index. When a trade note, a forecast,
        or a Slack screenshot folds three different counts into one headline, I
        pull them apart. Background-check volume is weather. The RetailBI
        Firearm Sales Index is what a reporting panel rang up. Search intent —
        including the zeros — is what people tried to find and often did not.
      </p>
      <p>
        Those zeros never become a unit. They still happened. If you only read
        the print, you will plan next season from a map of last season’s camp.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="mt-10">
      <p
        class="text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.14em] text-sky-400 mb-3"
      >
        The three, on separate lines
      </p>
      <ThreeNumbersTable />
    </div>

    <div
      class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-[1.05rem] leading-[1.7] text-zinc-300 font-serif"
    >
      <p>
        I cite the Index only with a date and a source on the same page. I do
        not pretend Coriolis sits in Gearfire’s Sisense. I do not run NICS. The
        live ask-side, when I point at it, is{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.betsyLive} class={linkClass} {...ext}>Betsy Live</a>
        , and I label it a sample.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you already buy sell-through, the missing layer is still the ask. The
        comparison of those two factories lives on GunSearchEngine, not here:
        {" "}
        <a href={LINKS.fortress} class={linkClass} {...ext}
          >RetailBI and Betsy, side by side</a
        >. Dealers who want the sensor on their own site start at{" "}
        <a href={LINKS.gsa} class={linkClass} {...ext}>GunSearchAgent</a>.
      </p>
    </div>

    <p class="mt-10">
      <LegalNote />
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
